TIP:  If transposing, play the root chord of the transposed (CaddG) adding the 5th note as necessary.

TIP:  In the intro, begin the first and last chord of each couplet by focusing on the root note.  For the (D) it's the 4th string.

TIP:  There's a tricky little voicing at the end of some lines.  For the untransposed it begins with a strum of |G| on the last word of the previous line and is followed by a single strum of |G| - |D|.  Then there's sort of a place holder to keep the timing indicated by the (a) which means come up and grab or strum the 5th string/5th - 4th - 3rd strings together.  Again, this is just to keep the rhythm.  Listen and you'll hear it.

 TIP:  As for the preaching bit, it goes over the hallelujahs of the choir with a 1, 1-2 count.  It's pretty hard to sing/speak both parts so play it however you want.
 
  
